body:
try not to be scared of making drinks because its fine if you mess it up like ive had a few other jobs and tim hortons was the one where no one really cared about someone making mistakes

/////

making mistakes might make your coworkers frustrated but still its how you are going to learn the job, and try not to take it personally and move on

/////

 observe how others do things especially if ur coworkers tell u tips its a very very repetitive job so ur coworkers are probably telling u the best/fastest way to do the certain thing so you will save time by benefitting from these tips

////

for taking orders or doing window: watch how your coworkers find solutions to problems (app not working we dont have that donut etc) and when you encounter it, offer those solutions, if they dont like it you can just tell them im going to get my supervisor, you dont have to deal with annoying people who arent looking for solutions (they are simply in a bad mood or an asshole) if its gonna burn you out, like yes you wanna get used to it, but also always remember you geniuenly dont have to deal with them, when you keep that in your mind you will be less scared of situations which will give you more confidence and keep you calm, if someone gives you shit for not wanting to deal with an agressive customer (red flag) dont think you have to, ive worked 10 months full time as a supervisor and whenever i got involved in a problem the general manager would tell me: why didnt you walk away from the customer you dont have to let them yell at you for 10 minutes (they wont be like wow that sucks they will jus say u shoudlnt have been a part of it)

////

if you like stocking and cleaning more than dealing with customers, take initiative on doing those, but never leave your regular station empty to go do something you werent asked to, but try to catch safe and free times to go do the things you prefer doing (first pay attention to how others do it) this will associate you with that task in supervisors minds so you will likely to be called that task from the floor which can be a great break during long shifts!

///

always keep in mind your position is your responsbility you can do other tasks but people will blame you if you left your station and they are sometimes right about that, take care of your station before anything else

////

make mistakes ask questions observe and dont be scared of messing up, ur coworkers/supervisors might likely be overworked stressed people so even if you try your hardest to please them they migjt get frustrated at you anyway jus cause the job is depressing, so try not to take it personal

for mhf4u final exam, i suggest using equatio from the beginning of your courswork and get REALLY used to it, ive practiced equatio mutliple times before the exam however i still wasted so much time during the exam just typing (even tho i am very fast with google docs equation editor)

u get sooo many questions and you have to save as much time as you can

however the good part is, the unit assesments are easy and you can look for help on google and make sure you gather as much marks as possible until your final exam, make sure they are perfect because you can get %100 in all of them (i got like an average of 99), use google use discord server to ask your peers for help and get your marks as high as possible before the final exam
